From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lemelson <97357844+Lemelson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:07:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] decoder: resume a paused video output from ChangePause

On resume after a paused seek with VideoToolbox, the video decoder can
block in pic_pacer_WaitAllocatableSlot(): the picture slots are held by
the paused video output (LLDB: pacer full, paused=0, output_paused=1,
frames_countdown=0). The DecoderThread loop that would resume the
output is never reached, because the decoder is blocked waiting for a
slot that only the resumed output can release. Playback stays frozen.

In vlc_input_decoder_ChangePause(false), resume a paused video output
directly with the existing Decoder_ChangeOutputPause() helper, under
the FIFO lock and only for VIDEO_ES with output_paused set. The
DecoderThread loop still acknowledges the new pause date as before
(on_output_paused is emitted there). Nothing is flushed or discarded;
audio and SPU are unchanged.

Note for review: this relaxes the documented rule that only the
DecoderThread drives the outputs while the decoder runs; the input
thread now calls vout_ChangePause() while holding the FIFO lock. Output
replacement by the ModuleThread is serialized by the same lock, and
the ownership comment is updated accordingly. Upstream may prefer to
fix the root cause (pacer slots held by a paused vout) differently;
this patch should then be dropped.

Reproduction: as in the decoder first-picture patch, with VideoToolbox
and AUHAL, then resume: video stays frozen and the decoder thread is
parked in pic_pacer_WaitAllocatableSlot(). Covered by
redesign/patches/engine/tests/run-paused-seek-smoke.sh (videotoolbox
auhal video).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/input/decoder.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/input/decoder.c b/src/input/decoder.c
index 514bc80..403af31 100644
--- a/src/input/decoder.c
+++ b/src/input/decoder.c
@@ -208,6 +208,8 @@ struct vlc_input_decoder_t
      *
      * The input thread can read these variables in order to stop outputs, when
      * both ModuleThread and DecoderThread are stopped (from DecoderDelete()).
+     * It can also resume a paused video output while holding the FIFO lock;
+     * ModuleThread output replacement is serialized by that same lock.
      */
      union {
         struct decoder_video video;
@@ -2899,6 +2901,11 @@ void vlc_input_decoder_ChangePause( vlc_input_decoder_t *p_owner,
     p_owner->paused = b_paused;
     p_owner->pause_date = i_date;
     p_owner->frames_countdown = 0;
+    /* An asynchronous decoder can be waiting for picture slots held by the
+     * paused output. Resume it here so the decoder can acknowledge the date
+     * in its normal loop; no picture is flushed or discarded. */
+    if (!b_paused && p_owner->cat == VIDEO_ES && p_owner->output_paused)
+        Decoder_ChangeOutputPause(p_owner, false, i_date);
     vlc_fifo_Signal( p_owner->p_fifo );
     vlc_fifo_Unlock( p_owner->p_fifo );
 }
